1
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:29,760
Shigemura, Shigemura, Shigemura, Shigemura

2
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:41,140
Oh, my God.

3
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:27,680
I don't know.

4
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:56,000
Oh, Asuna, I've turned into
the biggest crybaby, haven't I?

5
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,840
The feeling is rising,

6
00:02:03,940 --> 00:02:07,980
It's a true promise to me.

7
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:23,420
A miracle that I want,

8
00:02:24,720 --> 00:02:27,577
It's the end of the series!

9
00:02:27,660 --> 00:02:28,537
It's not our end.

10
00:02:28,620 --> 00:02:31,397
It's not our end.

11
00:02:31,480 --> 00:02:32,360
I'll be there.

12
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,197
We're not going to see the future.

13
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:40,537
I can't see the future.

14
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:41,917
We can't see the future.

15
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,377
We're not going to see the future.

16
00:02:43,460 --> 00:02:44,290
I'm going to see the future!

17
00:02:44,373 --> 00:02:45,203
But I'm still asking.

18
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:47,517
I'm singing.

19
00:03:14,760 --> 00:03:17,466
Ah, I'm going to spread
my eyes in the future!

20
00:03:18,220 --> 00:03:19,277
I'm going to spread

21
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,197
my eyes

22
00:03:20,280 --> 00:03:27,280
in

23
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:42,200
the future.

24
00:03:50,100 --> 00:03:51,276
I'm off to practice.

25
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:53,171
I'll see you later, okay?

26
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:41,497
Good morning.

27
00:04:41,580 --> 00:04:42,698
Good morning, Sugu.

28
00:04:46,340 --> 00:04:47,540
Good morning!

29
00:04:50,180 --> 00:04:51,460
God, seriously?

30
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:54,357
Instead of lurking, you
should have said something.

31
00:04:54,440 --> 00:04:58,260
Yeah, well, you were practicing
and I didn't want to bother you.

32
00:04:58,520 --> 00:05:00,240
I wasn't really practicing.

33
00:05:00,720 --> 00:05:02,544
I guess it's just habit is all.

34
00:05:04,580 --> 00:05:05,410
Oh.

35
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,339
At least you've been keeping it up.

36
00:05:10,100 --> 00:05:10,980
It's light.

37
00:05:12,060 --> 00:05:12,890
What?

38
00:05:12,973 --> 00:05:13,803
It's not light.

39
00:05:13,886 --> 00:05:14,998
It's timber bamboo.

40
00:05:15,560 --> 00:05:16,960
Oh, yeah, right.

41
00:05:17,380 --> 00:05:20,760
I meant, like, it's
lighter than I thought.

42
00:05:21,340 --> 00:05:23,575
It's not as heavy as what I'm used to.

43
00:05:28,180 --> 00:05:30,300
What the heck's he comparing it to?

44
00:05:33,740 --> 00:05:35,697
Hey, you think maybe
we could give it a go?

45
00:05:35,780 --> 00:05:37,133
What, you mean a match?

46
00:05:37,320 --> 00:05:38,380
Like, seriously?

47
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:39,830
Yep.

48
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:42,140
A real match with pads and stuff.

49
00:05:43,440 --> 00:05:46,100
Mmm, yeah, on second thought, no contact.

50
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:49,738
I mean, I'd feel like crap
if I ended up hurting you.

51
00:05:50,960 --> 00:05:53,380
I still gotta dig out Grandpa's old gear.

52
00:05:53,720 --> 00:05:55,485
How about we spar in the dojo?

53
00:05:55,720 --> 00:06:00,860
Whoa, you sound pretty darn confident for
someone who's been asleep for two years.

54
00:06:01,180 --> 00:06:05,768
For your information, I was a quarter-finalist
in the Middle School Nationals.

55
00:06:07,160 --> 00:06:10,297
Seriously, though, are you
sure you're feeling up to this?

56
00:06:10,380 --> 00:06:12,204
You might want to take it easy.

57
00:06:15,120 --> 00:06:19,767
I've been doing rehab in the gym every
day, so I think I'm gonna be good to go.

58
00:06:33,300 --> 00:06:35,829
What kind of stance is
that supposed to be?

59
00:06:36,140 --> 00:06:37,640
Don't you worry about it.

60
00:06:37,880 --> 00:06:39,380
This is my own style.

61
00:06:40,980 --> 00:06:43,160
Okay. Ready? Uh-huh.

62
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,840
His head's wide open.

63
00:06:49,220 --> 00:06:50,900
That'll be my first strike.

64
00:06:53,560 --> 00:06:54,390
Huh?

65
00:06:54,473 --> 00:06:57,580
It's an odd stance, but he looks composed.

66
00:07:06,300 --> 00:07:07,440
Okay, then.

67
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,620
Oh my god, are you okay?

68
00:07:39,640 --> 00:07:41,320
Okay, okay, you win.

69
00:07:41,900 --> 00:07:43,429
You sure are strong, Sugu.

70
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,918
You'd mop the floor with Heathcliff.

71
00:07:46,560 --> 00:07:49,560
Maybe you should sit down
or something. I'm good.

72
00:07:50,120 --> 00:07:51,355
Thanks for the match.

73
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:54,690
Huh?

74
00:08:04,480 --> 00:08:07,460
Did I hit you too hard? No, I'm okay.

75
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,996
Just years of habit.

76
00:08:11,860 --> 00:08:15,154
Let's see, my footwork was
okay, but the attacks sucked.

77
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:19,757
I guess I can't use the sword skills I
acquired unless I got the system helping.

78
00:08:19,840 --> 00:08:21,958
I have to say, I'm really surprised.

79
00:08:22,060 --> 00:08:25,413
I mean, how long have you been
practicing behind my back?

80
00:08:25,700 --> 00:08:28,320
Oh, you know, it is kind of fun after all.

81
00:08:28,640 --> 00:08:32,020
But you never know, maybe
I'll take it up again. Really?

82
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,500
Oh, seriously? Yeah, sure.

83
00:08:34,880 --> 00:08:36,337
You want to be my teacher?

84
00:08:36,420 --> 00:08:37,337
Are you kidding?

85
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,250
Of course.

86
00:08:38,380 --> 00:08:40,297
We'll train together like we used to.

87
00:08:40,380 --> 00:08:43,360
After I build up some more muscle, okay?

88
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,449
I've been practicing, too.

89
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,780
Want to know what? Huh?

90
00:08:52,320 --> 00:08:54,040
Nope, I'll keep it a secret.

91
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,860
That is so not cool.

92
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,780
You going anywhere today? Oh.

93
00:09:04,020 --> 00:09:04,980
I don't know.

94
00:09:05,260 --> 00:09:06,717
I guess...

95
00:09:06,800 --> 00:09:07,780
the hospital?

96
00:09:13,460 --> 00:09:15,257
Oh, you are. That's nice.

97
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:17,397
Her name's Asuna, right?

98
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:19,560
You visit her a lot.

99
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:22,130
Uh-huh.

100
00:09:22,213 --> 00:09:23,043
As much as I can.

101
00:09:23,126 --> 00:09:25,176
It's the only thing I can do for her.

102
00:09:26,780 --> 00:09:29,780
Anyway, Sugu, it's my turn
to make breakfast today.

103
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:32,797
It'll be ready by the time
you finish your shower.

104
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:33,710
Okay.

105
00:09:40,620 --> 00:09:43,267
It's been two months
since I beat Heathcliff,

106
00:09:43,700 --> 00:09:46,020
two months since I beat the Death Game.

107
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:52,673
When I woke up, I talked to someone
from the Ministry of Internal Affairs.

108
00:09:53,280 --> 00:09:55,860
I told them everything I knew about SAO,

109
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:59,160
and in exchange, they
told me where Asuna was.

110
00:10:06,240 --> 00:10:09,040
I found out she was nearby in Saitama.

111
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:13,332
Asuna's family admitted her
to Tokoazawa General Hospital.

112
00:10:16,420 --> 00:10:18,900
I also found out that besides her,

113
00:10:19,140 --> 00:10:23,020
there's about 300 other players
who haven't woken up yet.

114
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:30,940
Akihiko Kayaba's still missing,

115
00:10:31,260 --> 00:10:35,789
and people think he's keeping the players
in their comas as part of his plan.

116
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:40,280
SAO isn't over, not by a long shot.

117
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:54,750
Asuna.

118
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:05,330
Kazuto.

119
00:11:05,413 --> 00:11:07,139
Sorry, I didn't know you were here.

120
00:11:07,480 --> 00:11:08,715
Thank you for coming.

121
00:11:09,400 --> 00:11:10,580
Hello, Mr. Yuki.

122
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:12,529
I hope it's okay I'm here.

123
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:15,480
Please, you can visit whenever you like.

124
00:11:15,900 --> 00:11:17,460
I know it makes her happy.

125
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:25,650
Sir.

126
00:11:28,440 --> 00:11:31,205
Oh, I don't think the
two of you have ever met.

127
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:32,460
This is Sugo.

128
00:11:32,760 --> 00:11:34,900
He's our company's director of R &D.

129
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:36,960
I'm Nobuyuki Sugo.

130
00:11:37,260 --> 00:11:38,220
It's a pleasure.

131
00:11:39,260 --> 00:11:41,200
I'm Kazuto Kirigaya.

132
00:11:42,400 --> 00:11:43,960
You're THE Kirito?

133
00:11:44,160 --> 00:11:46,020
You're a hero. It's an honor.

134
00:11:46,800 --> 00:11:48,160
Oh, I'm sorry.

135
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:52,911
I know we're not supposed to talk about
what happened inside the SAO server.

136
00:11:53,020 --> 00:11:55,373
But he's my partner's son, so it's fine.

137
00:11:55,640 --> 00:11:58,993
Besides, I've always thought
of him as part of my family.

138
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:03,380
Actually, sir, speaking of family,

139
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:07,320
if I may, I'd like to make it
official as soon as possible.

140
00:12:08,460 --> 00:12:09,560
This is sudden.

141
00:12:10,060 --> 00:12:12,497
Are you sure this is really what you want?

142
00:12:12,580 --> 00:12:14,168
I mean, you're still young.

143
00:12:14,360 --> 00:12:16,437
You have your whole life ahead of you.

144
00:12:16,520 --> 00:12:19,638
Thank you for your concern,
but my heart's set on it.

145
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:24,993
It sounds strange, but even though
she's like this, she's still beautiful.

146
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:27,771
I'd like to see her in that wedding dress!

147
00:12:29,300 --> 00:12:30,460
You have a point.

148
00:12:31,980 --> 00:12:35,686
The sooner we prepare ourselves
for the inevitable, the better.

149
00:12:38,660 --> 00:12:40,617
Sorry to cut the conversation short.

150
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,420
I have a meeting to get to.

151
00:12:42,960 --> 00:12:45,180
We can talk more about this later.

152
00:12:46,820 --> 00:12:48,160
Kazuto, take care.

153
00:12:58,820 --> 00:13:01,700
I heard you and Asuna
were lovers in the game.

154
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:03,040
Is that true?

155
00:13:04,360 --> 00:13:05,190
Uh-huh.

156
00:13:05,580 --> 00:13:06,756
That is unfortunate.

157
00:13:07,180 --> 00:13:11,298
It's going to make for one complicated
relationship between you and I.

158
00:13:18,840 --> 00:13:24,620
In case you're curious, her father and
I were discussing her marriage to me.

159
00:13:27,800 --> 00:13:28,780
No way.

160
00:13:29,200 --> 00:13:30,760
You can't do that.

161
00:13:31,140 --> 00:13:32,340
You have a point.

162
00:13:32,720 --> 00:13:34,980
It's true, we can't legally marry.

163
00:13:35,220 --> 00:13:39,720
But if the Yuki family adopts me, it'll
be as if we are, on paper that is.

164
00:13:40,140 --> 00:13:41,680
Just like we're married.

165
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,160
The truth is, she's always hated
me, ever since we were kids.

166
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,155
Neither my parents nor hers know that.

167
00:13:49,500 --> 00:13:53,853
If I proposed and she could speak, I'm
pretty sure her answer would be no.

168
00:13:54,760 --> 00:13:58,980
For me, this situation is very favorable.

169
00:14:00,340 --> 00:14:01,320
Stop it!

170
00:14:05,840 --> 00:14:07,640
Who do you think you are?

171
00:14:07,900 --> 00:14:10,500
You can't take advantage
of Asuna like this.

172
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:12,200
Take advantage?

173
00:14:12,620 --> 00:14:13,577
Oh, please.

174
00:14:13,660 --> 00:14:16,380
If anything, I have a right to her.

175
00:14:17,220 --> 00:14:19,140
Perhaps I should explain why.

176
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:22,960
Any idea what happened to Argus?

177
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:25,940
They're the company that developed SAO.

178
00:14:26,260 --> 00:14:29,240
I heard they closed it down. Very good.

179
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:33,720
The lawsuits and damages they
had to pay took their toll.

180
00:14:34,240 --> 00:14:36,534
The company was forced into bankruptcy.

181
00:14:36,940 --> 00:14:41,000
But the maintenance of the SAO
servers was given to another company.

182
00:14:41,680 --> 00:14:46,740
An electronics manufacturer where
Asuna's father, Shozo Yuki, is the CEO.

183
00:14:47,600 --> 00:14:48,820
Wrecked progress.

184
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:53,800
And I work for the company's
full-dive technology R &D division.

185
00:14:54,420 --> 00:14:57,420
In other words, and without
getting into specifics,

186
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:01,000
you could say I'm the
one keeping Asuna alive.

187
00:15:01,800 --> 00:15:06,660
Now I ask you, is it wrong for me to expect
a little compensation for my trouble?

188
00:15:08,020 --> 00:15:11,397
I don't know what kind of promises
you made to each other in the game,

189
00:15:11,480 --> 00:15:12,892
and I don't really care.

190
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:16,600
But I don't ever want to see
you here again! Understood?

191
00:15:17,720 --> 00:15:20,960
And from now on, stay
away from the Yuki family.

192
00:15:21,640 --> 00:15:25,457
We're having the ceremony here
on January 26th, a week from now!

193
00:15:25,540 --> 00:15:26,820
Save the date.

194
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:30,477
Even though you're not welcome here
anymore, you should come to the wedding.

195
00:15:30,560 --> 00:15:32,280
No need to thank me.

196
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:35,790
Well, Mr.

197
00:15:35,873 --> 00:15:36,703
Hero

198
00:15:36,786 --> 00:15:38,677
You've got the room all to yourself now.

199
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:40,400
Say goodbye and get out.

200
00:15:47,640 --> 00:15:48,470
Kazuto!

201
00:15:48,760 --> 00:15:50,231
The bathroom's all yours!

202
00:15:58,340 --> 00:15:59,680
Jeez, what's wrong?

203
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,637
Why didn't you say something?

204
00:16:01,720 --> 00:16:04,380
And turn on the heat,
it's freezing in here!

205
00:16:09,820 --> 00:16:13,177
Sorry I just want to be left alone.

206
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:15,789
Hey how come you didn't
turn the heater on?

207
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:18,637
What's wrong are you okay?

208
00:16:18,720 --> 00:16:20,937
Yeah it's nothing.

209
00:16:21,020 --> 00:16:25,900
Okay but you're freezing
you're gonna catch a cold.

210
00:16:26,560 --> 00:16:28,940
I could run you a hot bath if you want.

211
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:35,857
I'm so hopeless and weak
I didn't want you to see

212
00:16:35,940 --> 00:16:38,877
this I swore no matter
what you'd never see me.

213
00:16:38,960 --> 00:16:40,137
Being such a crybaby

214
00:16:40,220 --> 00:16:46,757
is it Asuna is

215
00:16:46,840 --> 00:16:50,160
she okay did something happen to her?

216
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:53,737
She's leaving.

217
00:16:53,820 --> 00:16:56,257
Somewhere far away.

218
00:16:56,340 --> 00:16:58,137
And I'll never.

219
00:16:58,220 --> 00:17:00,820
I'm never gonna see her again.

220
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,450
Hey?

221
00:17:19,533 --> 00:17:21,300
Hey, hang in there, okay?

222
00:17:21,800 --> 00:17:26,260
If you really love someone that
much, even when things look hopeless,

223
00:17:26,540 --> 00:17:27,640
you can't give up.

224
00:17:32,820 --> 00:17:34,440
I know I can't.

225
00:17:36,840 --> 00:17:39,300
And I won't lie to myself anymore.

226
00:17:46,980 --> 00:17:49,680
Gosh, I remember it like it was yesterday.

227
00:17:51,240 --> 00:17:52,837
Kazuto stood there looking at me,

228
00:17:52,920 --> 00:17:56,685
and then he told me he wanted to
know who his real parents were.

229
00:17:56,780 --> 00:17:59,368
I was so shocked, I
didn't know what to say.

230
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:01,735
He was only ten, but here's the thing.

231
00:18:02,060 --> 00:18:06,648
Somehow, he logged onto the Citizen's
Registration Network and found the file.

232
00:18:07,380 --> 00:18:08,320
That figures.

233
00:18:08,960 --> 00:18:10,937
Sounds just like something he'd do.

234
00:18:11,020 --> 00:18:14,255
I was so stunned, I couldn't
think of a way to deny it.

235
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:16,232
So what do I do instead?

236
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:20,097
I tell him how my big sister and
her husband are his real parents.

237
00:18:20,180 --> 00:18:21,010
Wow.

238
00:18:23,800 --> 00:18:26,540
Mom, I was wondering. About what?

239
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:30,417
I guess about the way he's
been since middle school.

240
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,597
He'd go into his room and
play games online for hours.

241
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,457
You think it's because he found
out about his real parents?

242
00:18:36,540 --> 00:18:37,577
No, not at all.

243
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:40,248
He was always into
computers and technology.

244
00:18:40,520 --> 00:18:44,817
By the time he was six, he'd already
built his own computer out of spare parts.

245
00:18:44,900 --> 00:18:48,997
If anything, he's like that because
he's a huge computer nerd like me.

246
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,400
Or so he thinks.

247
00:18:52,900 --> 00:18:55,488
Well, I'm heading home
and get dinner ready.

248
00:18:55,580 --> 00:18:57,860
Don't stay too long, okay, Suguha?

249
00:18:58,500 --> 00:19:00,220
Don't worry. I won't.

250
00:19:05,600 --> 00:19:06,940
Happy birthday, kiddo.

251
00:19:14,920 --> 00:19:16,117
He's my cousin.

252
00:19:16,200 --> 00:19:18,120
Not my big brother.

253
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:21,120
I still have a hard time. Believing it.

254
00:19:24,440 --> 00:19:25,800
My big brother.

255
00:19:54,160 --> 00:19:56,600
But, in the end, your heart.

256
00:20:03,020 --> 00:20:04,980
In the end, your heart.

257
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:07,760
Belongs to her.

258
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:19,977
Come on!

259
00:20:20,060 --> 00:20:21,517
Wake up, Sugu!

260
00:20:21,600 --> 00:20:23,060
It's morning.

261
